[{:db/id "q-95054/selection/87b1d05596782ae1e8819b3f58922ba983d6bad6b4a163504412d1c9ea5d0ec7" :answer/id #uuid "7bc1bfd2-c1c3-5af7-9c5a-2193c87db66d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}{e}^{t}+2}{{e}^{t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95054/selection/4625bbb1f1587f1e0385e44fccdc9b209f140c33c5252695b2b0951cbf1893b4" :answer/id #uuid "0ea4fc8e-6262-5c15-b708-e3f49fdae9f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3({t}^{2}+1)}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95054/selection/3e10c9bf496cd8c66b17e49e9a7ae5ae7199feb22976a6d1840217c918c7ff56" :answer/id #uuid "f97111b5-dd1c-55c3-ab68-0babf0986b51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(t{e}^{t}-1)}{{e}^{t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95054/selection/b36d27c1398335a081b5b473a61ab8accbfb4efcf69e2ad84100e06a15a500ee" :answer/id #uuid "849e789f-60b6-505a-aa7f-d6d470de447a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t(t-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95054/selection/c80e49e9ec76f1a1a1bfe4d8d65bbd726790a779ab5dd6d032550818d2b36408" :answer/id #uuid "a4a268c7-a832-5168-bf38-ddba2a9f0377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(t-1)}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95054/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bc5a18f-d61b-574c-900b-359754d1aac9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95054/selection/c80e49e9ec76f1a1a1bfe4d8d65bbd726790a779ab5dd6d032550818d2b36408" :answer-field/choices ["q-95054/selection/87b1d05596782ae1e8819b3f58922ba983d6bad6b4a163504412d1c9ea5d0ec7" "q-95054/selection/4625bbb1f1587f1e0385e44fccdc9b209f140c33c5252695b2b0951cbf1893b4" "q-95054/selection/3e10c9bf496cd8c66b17e49e9a7ae5ae7199feb22976a6d1840217c918c7ff56" "q-95054/selection/b36d27c1398335a081b5b473a61ab8accbfb4efcf69e2ad84100e06a15a500ee" "q-95054/selection/c80e49e9ec76f1a1a1bfe4d8d65bbd726790a779ab5dd6d032550818d2b36408"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95054" :question/id #uuid "27f468d8-4b5c-529a-bb62-7538b371c44c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95054" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2})$ and $r(t)={t}^{-2}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{2xy}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+\\frac{2}{y}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={t}^{-2}$ and $y={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{-2}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{{e}^{t}}\\,j \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\,i+2{e}^{-t}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{-2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =-2{t}^{-3}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}\\,i+2{e}^{-t}\\,j)\\cdot (-2{t}^{-3}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =-2({t}^{2})({t}^{-3})+2{e}^{-t}({e}^{t}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{2}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(t-1)}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95054/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0096e314-e53e-5d9b-9cee-fe34fa3a6379"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37099/selection/4671fc399d4444f0d94f2daa6cc0353911e5f19ccb70f8b1efdc4ab9fdfd40c4" :answer/id #uuid "ae6a14e4-3252-5aac-aa2e-afa2e40f0dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t}-9{t}^{3}-36{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37099/selection/c08428488afcb8e427777ec008ce37d5fb61b842ef0978eddcf050fd437318c6" :answer/id #uuid "70ae4592-4444-5a9f-850d-9ffe3061926c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+9{t}^{3}+6{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37099/selection/59fdb3dd3b568f3cd1009c5861faba0966b77da53bf30fac11926c396a71a883" :answer/id #uuid "2dd9c594-257e-55af-8959-feb0d2509580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t}-9{t}^{2}-12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37099/selection/06ee1ec9e43642704e2c2cb05a27ad60a50b26b9c720607ae3100ee29ee165c6" :answer/id #uuid "0bdc5a08-c7db-523a-961a-d65f281389d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t}-3t-3t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37099/selection/7491f17cf438a2b58705b88000976519dbf60c9f64014f85376e895fab2ac290" :answer/id #uuid "55fd4168-b3ee-542c-8ea2-e5780fe4bd04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t}-3{t}^{2}+36{t}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37099/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "955b3a55-cc7d-5faa-aecf-cf559fa8a92f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37099/selection/4671fc399d4444f0d94f2daa6cc0353911e5f19ccb70f8b1efdc4ab9fdfd40c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-37099/selection/4671fc399d4444f0d94f2daa6cc0353911e5f19ccb70f8b1efdc4ab9fdfd40c4" "q-37099/selection/c08428488afcb8e427777ec008ce37d5fb61b842ef0978eddcf050fd437318c6" "q-37099/selection/59fdb3dd3b568f3cd1009c5861faba0966b77da53bf30fac11926c396a71a883" "q-37099/selection/06ee1ec9e43642704e2c2cb05a27ad60a50b26b9c720607ae3100ee29ee165c6" "q-37099/selection/7491f17cf438a2b58705b88000976519dbf60c9f64014f85376e895fab2ac290"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37099" :question/id #uuid "5e6f5348-317c-5ee8-9dde-644babe3a363" :question/math-academy-id "q-37099" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=2x-x{y}^{2}$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x-x{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x-x{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2-{y}^{2})\\,i-2xy\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t$ and $y=3{t}^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2-9{t}^{4})\\,i-6{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+6t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((2-9{t}^{4})\\,i-6{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+6t\\,j) \\\\  & =(2-9{t}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+(-6{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\cdot 6t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{t}-9{t}^{3}-36{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-37099/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0096e314-e53e-5d9b-9cee-fe34fa3a6379"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37099"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36211"] :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ and $r(t)={e}^{t}\\,i+{e}^{-t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2x\\,i+2y\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{t}$ and $y={e}^{-t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =2{e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{-t}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i-{e}^{-t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(2{e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{-t}\\,j)\\cdot ({e}^{t}\\,i-{e}^{-t}\\,j) \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}-2{e}^{-t}\\cdot {e}^{-t} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-95059/selection/822ec010cf00dbb949acbdbe8296b134f723dce1eda4a0cfdd366fd58c1415d2" :answer/id #uuid "391d959e-c74c-5024-8121-179d1433d76c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95059/selection/61b85bd106971cab08f9ff830aca28c564a0f05333e1a577bc62bc85d47ef75a" :answer/id #uuid "9055c435-f908-5297-b992-d625acd2891f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95059/selection/fe154427977d759670ea87bd10bed7d685c96e9f775d9028b7442faf68c9cf49" :answer/id #uuid "936e9953-ed9f-5188-8fc0-bc31ce9811fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95059/selection/297af6ca47919916089ff38623765c0056d0a4301f14b2c9565cd0920ee9a1e0" :answer/id #uuid "0246257f-4c69-5b21-aa42-8d995a779012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t}}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95059/selection/7b5544d5d0bd27e8176e691b8a7faa0c55368e18fb7fc811972c92cf51c020da" :answer/id #uuid "347b86e8-8cbc-5d3c-81c5-a6ec53000050" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95059/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2dee7e88-ad97-588e-bc6c-6b86d0cee975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95059/selection/61b85bd106971cab08f9ff830aca28c564a0f05333e1a577bc62bc85d47ef75a" :answer-field/choices ["q-95059/selection/822ec010cf00dbb949acbdbe8296b134f723dce1eda4a0cfdd366fd58c1415d2" "q-95059/selection/61b85bd106971cab08f9ff830aca28c564a0f05333e1a577bc62bc85d47ef75a" "q-95059/selection/fe154427977d759670ea87bd10bed7d685c96e9f775d9028b7442faf68c9cf49" "q-95059/selection/297af6ca47919916089ff38623765c0056d0a4301f14b2c9565cd0920ee9a1e0" "q-95059/selection/7b5544d5d0bd27e8176e691b8a7faa0c55368e18fb7fc811972c92cf51c020da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95059" :question/id #uuid "dc00486a-99d9-5db5-9476-31c56fe05627" :question/math-academy-id "q-95059" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡xy$ and $r(t)={e}^{t}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡xy)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡xy)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,j\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{t}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,i+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,i+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot ({e}^{t}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}+\\frac{{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}{1+{e}^{2t}{sin}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95059/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0096e314-e53e-5d9b-9cee-fe34fa3a6379"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95059"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95052/selection/934836c9ebd6cdb6db31c210887b06b64d71b9ad58e136def53184ff22714123" :answer/id #uuid "035467b8-67e8-5026-a1d6-6f815b3dbbfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95052/selection/683ccb4f8d078bebdca2e75e4f45174a3aa54767af125aaae641d8a23c9b3cd7" :answer/id #uuid "c73cded5-1254-567f-91cb-0917f236838d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95052/selection/d09bb8dd9d5b783d12e6aa27a47395cfbf97b29eed4a0f1a44926a2af50bb4ac" :answer/id #uuid "cd7159e2-fa67-5b6c-8cc8-99ae8262d8a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95052/selection/b1cb032bbe5d0a9c45721ecfaef1a21736dd296a998a8da3e3b816356eb844e1" :answer/id #uuid "b55b005b-49a4-58f7-a55d-51abe9a930fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95052/selection/b233af8e58a8925668370e083a0a015e8f1149a967cf892b9bcef9858e045944" :answer/id #uuid "2c0a906d-5e7e-5cee-a036-7920c431f3f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95052/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "faeb2d79-4b1f-5bff-bbbe-d5c88caa54ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95052/selection/b1cb032bbe5d0a9c45721ecfaef1a21736dd296a998a8da3e3b816356eb844e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-95052/selection/934836c9ebd6cdb6db31c210887b06b64d71b9ad58e136def53184ff22714123" "q-95052/selection/683ccb4f8d078bebdca2e75e4f45174a3aa54767af125aaae641d8a23c9b3cd7" "q-95052/selection/d09bb8dd9d5b783d12e6aa27a47395cfbf97b29eed4a0f1a44926a2af50bb4ac" "q-95052/selection/b1cb032bbe5d0a9c45721ecfaef1a21736dd296a998a8da3e3b816356eb844e1" "q-95052/selection/b233af8e58a8925668370e083a0a015e8f1149a967cf892b9bcef9858e045944"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95052" :question/id #uuid "5706cde4-4f11-53d8-86d6-e3542d0c8d21" :question/math-academy-id "q-95052" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $r(t)=\\pi t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,j \\\\  & =-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\pi t$ and $y={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\pi \\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j)\\cdot (\\pi \\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\pi {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95052/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0096e314-e53e-5d9b-9cee-fe34fa3a6379"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95052"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95070/selection/9a12f8be054b4a4f486d0a6c159e31b610941d4d7a6e6859ffdb1bcf72985773" :answer/id #uuid "e1acad9a-22fa-5b84-8e7b-95ae083525e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t{cos}^{3}⁡2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95070/selection/9536335838424e792c0748d606d49cb665ab157410ecd0ecf515692dfce9ae44" :answer/id #uuid "9c3b3fce-8426-5478-af3e-f931f78bf962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95070/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "14eae0bd-259f-5ab9-94b2-73214d4495b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95070/selection/febdc123cb10c90f96cbe5008ad38cb3b5296150f74720c840eaf06225c2629d" :answer/id #uuid "79e96f2e-f4ed-5a2d-80cd-70e1a6fc3e25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95070/selection/411ad34bd38df3d9869404bf85f1ef880983855d490e9c8a4b5f7f96045fd5c5" :answer/id #uuid "fb24c6bf-8f59-5ad5-bc42-c6bd85063a7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{3}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95070/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd104594-30e1-5f04-9f6d-17bc4507b3b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95070/selection/febdc123cb10c90f96cbe5008ad38cb3b5296150f74720c840eaf06225c2629d" :answer-field/choices ["q-95070/selection/9a12f8be054b4a4f486d0a6c159e31b610941d4d7a6e6859ffdb1bcf72985773" "q-95070/selection/9536335838424e792c0748d606d49cb665ab157410ecd0ecf515692dfce9ae44" "q-95070/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-95070/selection/febdc123cb10c90f96cbe5008ad38cb3b5296150f74720c840eaf06225c2629d" "q-95070/selection/411ad34bd38df3d9869404bf85f1ef880983855d490e9c8a4b5f7f96045fd5c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95070" :question/id #uuid "f21a3cf3-f1f0-5a46-96b4-1bd6124c44a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-95070" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)={x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+2t\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,k \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\,i-4{y}^{3}\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $z=2t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,i-4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,i-4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95070/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "112e3378-bde8-5896-822e-e815bde51501"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95142/selection/22aa6c85a45c73ffed05a71bb90b5513e5bfa2257b6ac7a12e4fcfed66fca076" :answer/id #uuid "e3e30df3-6a66-54f0-b876-5e9b34e40de2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4+4t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95142/selection/44b8bb6588c780a674122753c64027a472ce94629fba44fc48731e1f51c3ba59" :answer/id #uuid "1b089001-03e4-5ffa-abf8-58bf7db0ec96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95142/selection/b54ca8907e4e7fe2814902c22afab09041e330b1b89f6c90b17bdb7b177f29e7" :answer/id #uuid "f54f1257-b9e7-5979-a3ac-a46fba6cbd4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t(t-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95142/selection/1f70fc9cb9a98e8b47d751c0b67d39870fe7fc998196a7779e45f69da755b2e2" :answer/id #uuid "341cb5e6-d276-5321-9a1c-b7a87c3a3db5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t(t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95142/selection/3548a695fbdaa03f55b4f3c60f5ac0b36d712782e74c0dd61b898999a301c360" :answer/id #uuid "c4453b7e-40a6-5b08-8807-623206ced9d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95142/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4b7d0e8-79ee-54ac-8829-71baefe21a4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95142/selection/3548a695fbdaa03f55b4f3c60f5ac0b36d712782e74c0dd61b898999a301c360" :answer-field/choices ["q-95142/selection/22aa6c85a45c73ffed05a71bb90b5513e5bfa2257b6ac7a12e4fcfed66fca076" "q-95142/selection/44b8bb6588c780a674122753c64027a472ce94629fba44fc48731e1f51c3ba59" "q-95142/selection/b54ca8907e4e7fe2814902c22afab09041e330b1b89f6c90b17bdb7b177f29e7" "q-95142/selection/1f70fc9cb9a98e8b47d751c0b67d39870fe7fc998196a7779e45f69da755b2e2" "q-95142/selection/3548a695fbdaa03f55b4f3c60f5ac0b36d712782e74c0dd61b898999a301c360"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95142" :question/id #uuid "224ae8bf-e6ea-586d-bfd7-ecc0ca99a9f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95142" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+(t+1)\\,j+(t-1)\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}[x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})]\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}[x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})]\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}[x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})]\\,k \\\\  & =({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\,i+2xy\\,j-2xz\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ $y=t+1$ and $z=t-1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =[(t+1)^{2}-(t-1)^{2}]i+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot (t+1)\\,j-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot (t-1)\\,k \\\\  & =4t\\,i+2(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,j-2(t-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\,j+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(4t\\,i+2(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,j-2(t-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =4t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+2(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot 1-2(t-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4+2(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-2(t-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\  & =4+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95142/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "112e3378-bde8-5896-822e-e815bde51501"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95142"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95072/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2a530362-4294-508a-98ac-17ca1ba7bfa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95072/selection/ea26f875a29a024f0f8bacfa7a23507db00a8f5381867204e02e3fd29305e92b" :answer/id #uuid "66fbd59a-8621-5bbf-9cf0-e1a014dcd33c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2t+1}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95072/selection/3473db39c51596230dfceedd56e75ecb0561bfd3b6fbf4f618e42df55ffb660e" :answer/id #uuid "4dd125bd-c465-54a1-8bfe-5a14364b0336" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}+1}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95072/selection/236094ebfb17179688caf1aaef417fc98cd3850051a62efae3fd22e0fda611bb" :answer/id #uuid "4b07bbe3-ebd6-58bb-8745-80c0a06d4c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{t-1}(1-t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95072/selection/f66810a1c179114985519f39ffd5acd6021ff9bd5a7317674ca7d0fe7ab5e258" :answer/id #uuid "e25913f0-5f1c-5cde-982a-e61f65961d88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2t{e}^{t}+1}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95072/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3277f3-90ef-5524-9657-16f716199789" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95072/selection/ea26f875a29a024f0f8bacfa7a23507db00a8f5381867204e02e3fd29305e92b" :answer-field/choices ["q-95072/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-95072/selection/ea26f875a29a024f0f8bacfa7a23507db00a8f5381867204e02e3fd29305e92b" "q-95072/selection/3473db39c51596230dfceedd56e75ecb0561bfd3b6fbf4f618e42df55ffb660e" "q-95072/selection/236094ebfb17179688caf1aaef417fc98cd3850051a62efae3fd22e0fda611bb" "q-95072/selection/f66810a1c179114985519f39ffd5acd6021ff9bd5a7317674ca7d0fe7ab5e258"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95072" :question/id #uuid "62e98c0a-559d-53b0-94a4-7601b7fde1bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-95072" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)$ and $r(t)=t\\,i+{e}^{t-1}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{yz}{xyz}\\,i+\\frac{xz}{xyz}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{xyz}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+\\frac{1}{y}\\,j+\\frac{1}{z}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y={e}^{t-1},$ and $z={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t-1}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t-1})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & =i+{e}^{t-1}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t-1}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\,k)\\cdot (i+{e}^{t-1}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}+\\frac{{e}^{t-1}}{{e}^{t-1}}+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2t+1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95072/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "112e3378-bde8-5896-822e-e815bde51501"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95072"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95146/selection/85c7c9ebbc82f2132462de6e483703806c7dbaa0850f97a340e2063a2fd7d348" :answer/id #uuid "80eeaf50-465c-5002-9d48-33f912b73133" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95146/selection/ee20fb756f3f51ad05da5846d7f38db0593a2332e471746d340b87bd02a7d21b" :answer/id #uuid "9c71dcb7-db2e-568c-8b22-d82c48f2964c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95146/selection/fa7ddeab4d08832a7df4283a401af4cf88e62f157eab8a44bc199219761081d2" :answer/id #uuid "cd57d719-616b-5c6f-9d89-74e8481d68af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95146/selection/ec55817028957596edaeeb55b383129891ade713d2fa116c3f67868a7d082f00" :answer/id #uuid "19b35187-9ddc-5472-b0f9-4ed5d742675b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95146/selection/88abddd0ba29baf8a9bc2cfcc498c0438d5abda092cb1a8805870bf1ef2d5abe" :answer/id #uuid "d213d58e-0038-5389-9f4e-b44372101791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95146/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ac43510-dfda-5e7c-a541-725b288063d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95146/selection/88abddd0ba29baf8a9bc2cfcc498c0438d5abda092cb1a8805870bf1ef2d5abe" :answer-field/choices ["q-95146/selection/85c7c9ebbc82f2132462de6e483703806c7dbaa0850f97a340e2063a2fd7d348" "q-95146/selection/ee20fb756f3f51ad05da5846d7f38db0593a2332e471746d340b87bd02a7d21b" "q-95146/selection/fa7ddeab4d08832a7df4283a401af4cf88e62f157eab8a44bc199219761081d2" "q-95146/selection/ec55817028957596edaeeb55b383129891ade713d2fa116c3f67868a7d082f00" "q-95146/selection/88abddd0ba29baf8a9bc2cfcc498c0438d5abda092cb1a8805870bf1ef2d5abe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95146" :question/id #uuid "165b0f80-a698-5ec6-a618-8d8ca9054e5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95146" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,k \\\\  & =-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,j+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={t}^{2},y={e}^{t},$ and $z={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (2t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k) \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{t}+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}+2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-95146/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "112e3378-bde8-5896-822e-e815bde51501"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95146"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95149/selection/e15bb251da3066329dc9a26ee95d4eda937d623a67a6d78f3210db5a4535d96d" :answer/id #uuid "ee5e2852-1b69-5497-9391-71f0d8e0417b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\frac{{e}^{{t}^{2}}}{{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95149/selection/de2bb22ea24acfcb975ba309e78054725028fee382f47b7ee5ea8524da4c03b1" :answer/id #uuid "122fb1dd-9721-5a71-8d68-83ecf72ebeff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95149/selection/3ad3f9b0137bca14bfd52c734f938e58205dacef8ce480a69a376b1f82f46155" :answer/id #uuid "4dacc4b2-5e12-586a-a75d-3e38f72c13c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{e}^{{t}^{2}}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95149/selection/a2cdb5c995eed6e4e9780baaac0b0dab7e10b7c634f0eee75ec67dd66e29cc38" :answer/id #uuid "0beb897a-d545-5430-bc16-3ee297ccd3ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t+{e}^{{t}^{2}}+t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95149/selection/92538811bfbef9a612402795fea0411e56001b359a44a2ef17a428ee1c5aee07" :answer/id #uuid "5dacf331-e6e2-5b29-9a8e-f965950b92ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95149/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fd21708-f094-5c4d-9d0e-cb9e2f847f40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95149/selection/92538811bfbef9a612402795fea0411e56001b359a44a2ef17a428ee1c5aee07" :answer-field/choices ["q-95149/selection/e15bb251da3066329dc9a26ee95d4eda937d623a67a6d78f3210db5a4535d96d" "q-95149/selection/de2bb22ea24acfcb975ba309e78054725028fee382f47b7ee5ea8524da4c03b1" "q-95149/selection/3ad3f9b0137bca14bfd52c734f938e58205dacef8ce480a69a376b1f82f46155" "q-95149/selection/a2cdb5c995eed6e4e9780baaac0b0dab7e10b7c634f0eee75ec67dd66e29cc38" "q-95149/selection/92538811bfbef9a612402795fea0411e56001b359a44a2ef17a428ee1c5aee07"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95149" :question/id #uuid "6b9a1e6d-4a31-5f79-a94b-57b7a189c272" :question/math-academy-id "q-95149" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y}$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+{e}^{y}\\,j+\\frac{1}{z}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,y={t}^{2},$ and $z=\\frac{1}{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\,j+t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\,j+t\\,k)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95149/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "112e3378-bde8-5896-822e-e815bde51501"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95149"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37109/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "3a069963-